The subprocess port provides a modern C++23 cross-platform subprocess library
for Linux and Windows (supporting both `#include <subprocess/subprocess.hpp>` and
`import subprocess;`).

To use it, add the following to your CMakeLists.txt:

    find_package(subprocess CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(my-target PRIVATE subprocess::subprocess)

Optional vcpkg features:
    modules (enabled by default) - Build and install the C++23 module interface.
    skills                       - Install AI agent skill into share/agent-skills/subprocess.
